  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Given that f: x ↦ 3x − 2, g: x ↦ 2x + 5 and h: x ↦ (2x + 3)/(x − 1): (a) Evaluate (i) g(-6) and (ii) fg(3). (b) If f(x) = 8, calculate the value of x. (c) Obtain an expression, in terms of x, for h⁻¹(x)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Three skills are being tested: substituting into a function, composing two of them, and reversing one."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p141_q04.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p141-q04 from workbook page 141."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Evaluate g(-6).",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "g(-6) = 2(-6) + 5 = -12 + 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: g(-6) = -7"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Evaluate fg(3): apply g first, then f.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "g(3) = 2(3) + 5 = 11, then f(11) = 3(11) − 2 = 33 − 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: fg(3) = 31"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Solve f(x) = 8.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "3x − 2 = 8 → 3x = 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: x = 10/3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Set y = h(x) and clear the fraction.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "y(x − 1) = 2x + 3 → yx − y = 2x + 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: yx − 2x = y + 3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 5,
      "instruction": "Factor out x and divide.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "x(y − 2) = y + 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: x = (y + 3)/(y − 2)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 6,
      "instruction": "Write the inverse in terms of x.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Replace y by x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: h⁻¹(x) = (x + 3)/(x − 2), x ≠ 2"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Substitute directly for (a)(i), work inner-then-outer for (a)(ii), solve 3x − 2 = 8 for (b), and rearrange y = h(x) to make x the subject for (c)."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a)(i) g(-6) = -7  (a)(ii) fg(3) = 31  (b) x = 10/3  (c) h⁻¹(x) = (x + 3)/(x − 2), x ≠ 2."
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Every part rests on the same idea: a function is a rule turning an input into an output. Evaluating runs the rule forwards, solving f(x) = 8 runs it backwards for one particular output, and finding the inverse runs it backwards for every output at once. That is why parts (b) and (c) feel like the same algebra — they are."
    }
  ],
